      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 3,
      "description": "First project-side handoff of the exact malformed second RR slice into structured RR decoding. On iteration 1 this call presents `p = packet + 62`, `end - p = 2`, and trailing bytes `c0 0d`, while `packet_ctx` still carries the full packet and the label blocks accumulated from earlier RR names."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "R-COMPRESSED-POINTER-TARGET-BACKWARD",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "src/lib/util/dns.c",
      "function": "dns_label_decode",
      "line": 1159,
      "operands": [
        "buf + offset",
        "*start"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "buf + offset",
        "right": "*start"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "A-ROOT-COMPRESSED-POINTER-TARGET-BACKWARD",
      "fine_trace_step": 11,
      "description": "Root cause. On the second decode pass, only reachable because both prior length probes returned positive `48`, `dns_label_decode()` treats bytes `ff 20` as a compressed-label pointer, computes attacker-controlled offset `0x3f20`, and assigns `p = buf + offset` without checking that the target is backward and within the current packet extent. The patch adds packet/end arguments and rejects exactly these invalid targets before `*p` is used."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "N-SINK-DEREF-USES-FORWARD-RESOLVED-POINTER",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "src/lib/util/dns.c",
      "function": "dns_label_decode",
      "line": 1166,
      "operands": [
        "*start",
        "p"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "*start",
        "right": "p"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "A-SINK-DEREF-USES-FORWARD-RESOLVED-POINTER",
      "fine_trace_step": 12,
      "description": "ASan crash site. After step 11 sets `p` to `packet + 0x3f20`, this statement dereferences `*p` at that wild address to compute the next label pointer."
    },
